{
  "title": "34: Sabaa سبإ",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ وَهُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(1)\nAALHAMDU LILLAAHE LAZEE LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE LAHUL HAMDO FIL AAKHERATE WA HOWA HAKEEM KHABEER.\nAll praise is God’s, Whose is whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth, and His is all praise in the hereafter; and He is the All Wise, the All-Aware.\nيَعْلَمُ مَا يَلِجُ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا وَمَا يَنْزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيْهَا ؕ وَهُوَ الرَّحِيْمُ الْغَفُوْرُ‏(2)\nYA’LAMO MAA YALEJU FIL ARZE WA MAA YAKHROJO MINHAA WA MAA YANZELU MENAL SAMAAA-E WA MAA YAA’RUJU FEEHAA WA HOWA RAHEEM GHAFOORUL.\nKnoweth He whatever that passeth into the earth and whatever that cometh out of it, and whatever that cometh down from the heaven and whatever that goeth up unto it; and He is the Most Merciful, the Oft-Forgiving.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَا تَاْتِيْنَا السَّاعَةُ ؕ قُلْ بَلٰى وَرَبِّىْ لَتَاْتِيَنَّكُمْۙ عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ ۚ لَا يَعْزُبُ عَنْهُ مِثْقَالُ ذَرَّةٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَاۤ اَصْغَرُ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْبَرُ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(3)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAA TAATEENAA SAA-A’TO QUL BALAA WA RABBEE LATAATEENNAKUM A’ALEMIL GHAYBE LAA YAA’ZUBU A’NHO MESQAALU ZARRATIN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA LAA FIL ARZE WA LAA AASGHARU MIN ZAA LEKA WA LAA AKBARO ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nAnd say those who disbelieve: “The Hour (of Judgment) shall not come upon us.” Say thou: “Yea: By my Lord, the Knower of the unseen, it shall certainly come upon you, from Him is not hidden, the weight of (even) an atom in the heavens and nor in the earth, nor is there aught less than this and nor aught greater, but it is in the manifesting Book,\nلِّيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوْا الصّٰلِحٰتِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(4)\nLE-YAJZEYAL LAZEENA AAMANUT AAMANOO AS-SAALEHAATE OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WWAREZQUN KAREEM.\nThat He may recompense those who believe and do good; these it is for whom is forgiveness and an honourable sustenance.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ سَعَوْ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا مُعٰجِزِيْنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مِّنْ رِّجْزٍ اَلِيْمٌ‏(5)\nWAL LAZEENA SAA’AW FEE AAYAATENAA MUA’AAJEZEENA OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MIN RREJZIN ALEEM.\nAnd for those who strive hard in invalidating Our signs, these it is for whom is a chastisement of a painful torment.\nوَيَرَى الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ الَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ هُوَ الْحَقَّ ۙ وَيَهْدِىْۤ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَمِيْدِ‏(6)\nWA YARAL LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA LAZEE UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA HOWA HAQQA WA YAHDEE ELAA SERAATE A’ZEEZIL HAMEEDIL.\nAnd will see those whom knowledge hath been given, that which hath been sent down unto thee from thy Lord, that it is the truth, and it guideth unto the path of the All-Mighty, the Most Praised (One)\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا هَلْ نَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰى رَجُلٍ يُّنَبِّئُكُمْ اِذَا مُزِّقْتُمْ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍۙ اِنَّكُمْ لَفِىْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍۚ‏(7)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO HAL NADULLUKUM A’LAA RAJULIN YYUNABBEUKUM EZAA MUZZEQTUM KULLA MUMAZZAQIN INNAKUM LAFEE KHALQIN JADEEDIN.\nAnd say those who disbelieve, (in ridicule): “Shall we point out to you a man who informeth you that when ye are wholly scattered totally disintegrated, (even then) ye are certainly (returned) into a new creation?\nاَ فْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَمْ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ  ؕ بَلِ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ فِى الْعَذَابِ وَالضَّلٰلِ الْبَعِيْدِ‏(8)\nA’ZAABAN FTARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AM BEHI JENNATUN BALIL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE FIL A’ZAABE WAALZZALAALE AL-BAE’EEDE.\nHath he forged a lie against God or there is madness in him?” Nay! those who believe not in the hereafter are in a torment and are straying far (away from the truth)\nاَفَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلٰى مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ ؕ اِنْ نَّشَاْ نَخْسِفْ بِهِمُ الْاَرْضَ اَوْ نُسْقِطْ عَلَيْهِمْ كِسَفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُّنِيْبٍ‏(9)\nA-FALAM YARAW ELAA MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM MENAL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE IN NASHAA NAKHSEF BEHEMUL ARZA AW NUSQET A’LAYHIM KESAFAN MENAL SAMAAA-E INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEKULLE A’ABDIN MMUNEEBIN.\nSee they not then what is before them and what is behind them of the heaven and the earth? If We please We will make them sink into the earth or We bring down upon them a portion from the heaven; Verily in this is a sign for every servant turning (unto the Lord).\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ مِنَّا فَضْلًا ؕ يٰجِبَالُ اَوِّبِىْ مَعَهٗ وَالطَّيْرَ ۚ وَاَلَنَّا لَهُ الْحَدِيْدَ ۙ‏(10)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA DAAWOODA MINNAA FAZLAM YAAJEBAALU AAWBEAA MA-A’HU WA TAYRA WAALANNAA LAHUL AL-HADEEDA.\nAnd indeed gave We unto David from Us, a boon saying: “O’ Mountains! sing ye the praise of God along with him, and (ye) the birds (Too);” and made We soft for him, the iron,\nاَنِ اعْمَلْ سٰبِغٰتٍ وَّقَدِّرْ فِى السَّرْدِ وَاعْمَلُوْا صَالِحًا ؕ اِنِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(11)\nSAALEHAN AA’MAL SAABEGHAATIN WWAQADDER FIL AS-SARDE WAAA’MALOOA SAALEHAN INNEE BEMAA TA’MALOON BASEER.\nSaying (unto David): “Make thou coats of mail, and measure its links and do good; verily I, of what all ye do, do see.\nوَلِسُلَيْمٰنَ الرِّيْحَ غُدُوُّهَا شَهْرٌ وَّرَوَاحُهَا شَهْرٌۚ وَ اَسَلْنَا لَهٗ عَيْنَ الْقِطْرِؕ وَمِنَ الْجِنِّ مَنْ يَّعْمَلُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهِؕ وَمَنْ يَّزِغْ مِنْهُمْ عَنْ اَمْرِنَا نُذِقْهُ مِنْ عَذَابِ السَّعِيْرِ‏(12)\nWA LESOLAYMAANA AR-REEHA GHUDOOHAA SHAHRUN WWARAWAAHUHAA SHAHRUN WA AASALNAA LAHU A’YNAL AL-QETRE WA MENAN JINNE MAN YYAA’MALU BAYNA YADAYHE BE-IZNIL RABBEHE WA MAN YYAZEGH MINHUM A’N AAMRENAA NUZEQHU MIN A’ZAABIN SA-E’ER.\nAnd for Solomon (We made subservient) the wind which travelled in the morning a month’s journey and a month’s journey in the evening; And We caused for him to flow a fountain of molten brass and of the jinn there were those who worked before him by the command of his Lord; and whoever among them turned away from Our Command, We will make him taste, of the chastisement of the flaming fire.\nيَعْمَلُوْنَ لَهٗ مَا يَشَآءُ مِنْ مَّحَارِيْبَ وَتَمَاثِيْلَ وَجِفَانٍ كَالْجَوَابِ وَقُدُوْرٍ رّٰسِيٰتٍ ؕ اِعْمَلُوْۤا اٰلَ دَاوٗدَ شُكْرًا ؕ وَقَلِيْلٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىَ الشَّكُوْرُ‏(13)\nYA’MALOON LAHU MAA YASHAAA MIN MMAHAAREEBA WATAMAASEELA WAJEFAANIN KAALJAWAABE WAQUDOORIN RRAASEETIN AEA’MALOOA AALA DAAWOODA SHUKRAN WA QALEELUM MIN E’EBAADEAAA ASH-SHAKOORU.\nThey made for him whatever he willeth of fortresses and statues, and basins (large as) reservoirs, and (huge) cooking cauldrons immovable from their places; “Act ye gratefully, O’ family of David! and very few of My servants are grateful!\nفَلَمَّا قَضَيْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَوْتَ مَا دَلَّهُمْ عَلٰى مَوْتِهٖۤ اِلَّا دَآ بَّةُ الْاَرْضِ تَاْ كُلُ مِنْسَاَتَهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا خَرَّ تَبَيَّنَتِ الْجِنُّ اَنْ لَّوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ الْغَيْبَ مَا لَبِثُوْا فِى الْعَذَابِ الْمُهِيْنِ ؕ‏(14)\nFALAMMAA QAZAYNAA A’LAYHE MAWTA MAA DALLAHUM A’LAA MAWTEH ILLAA DAABBATINW BBATU ARZE TAA KULU MENSAATAHU FALAMMAA KHARRA TABAYNATE AL-JENNU AN LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON GHAYBA MAA MAA FIL A’ZAABE MOHEENE.\nAnd when We decreed death for him (Solomon), nothing did show them his death, but a worm of the earth which gnawed away his staff; and when it fell down, then came to know the jinn that had they known the unseen, they would have tarried not in the humiliating torment (of their toil)\nلَقَدْ كَانَ لِسَبَاٍ فِىْ مَسْكَنِهِمْ اٰيَةٌ  ۚ جَنَّتٰنِ عَنْ يَّمِيْنٍ وَّشِمَالٍ ؕ  کُلُوْا مِنْ رِّزْقِ رَبِّكُمْ وَاشْكُرُوْا لَهٗ ؕ بَلْدَةٌ طَيِّبَةٌ وَّرَبٌّ غَفُوْرٌ‏‏(15)\nLAQAD KAANA LE-SABA-IM FEE MASKANEHEM TAA-TEENAA JANNATAAN A’N YYAMEENIN WWASHEMAALIN LOOA MIN RIZQIL RABBEKUM WASH KOROO LAHU BALDATUN TAYBATUN WWARABBUN GHAFOORUR.\nIndeed for (the children of) Saba in their abode, there was a sign; two gardens on the right and the left; (and it was said unto them) “Eat ye of the sustenance of your Lord and give ye thanks unto Him”; A good land (it was, in this world) and (God is the) Lord Oft- Forgiving!\nفَاَعْرَضُوْا فَاَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَيْلَ الْعَرِمِ وَبَدَّلْنٰهُمْ بِجَنَّتَيْهِمْ جَنَّتَيْنِ ذَوَاتَىْ اُكُلٍ خَمْطٍ وَّاَثْلٍ وَّشَىْءٍ مِّنْ سِدْرٍ قَلِيْلٍ‏(16)\nFA A-A’RAZOO FA-ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM SAYLA AL-A’AREME WABADDALNAAHUM BEJANNATAYHEM JANNATAYNE ZAWAATAA AUKULIN KHAMTIN WWAASLIN WWASHAAIN MIN SIDRIM QALEELIN.\nBut they turned away, so sent We upon them a torrent irresistible and in place of their two gardens gave We unto them two gardens yielding bitter fruits and tamarisks and a few lote trees.\nذٰ لِكَ جَزَيْنٰهُمْ بِمَا كَفَرُوْا ؕ وَهَلْ نُجٰزِىْۤ اِلَّا الْكَفُوْرَ‏(17)\nZAA LEKA JAZAYNAAHUM BEMAA KAFAROO WA HAL NUJAAZEAA ILLAA AL-KAFOORA.\nThis We recompensed them for what they disbelieved; but do We (thus) recompense any save the ungrateful?\nوَجَعَلْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ الْقُرَى الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا قُرًى ظَاهِرَةً وَّقَدَّرْنَا فِيْهَا السَّيْرَ ؕ سِيْرُوْا فِيْهَا لَيَالِىَ وَاَيَّامًا اٰمِنِيْنَ‏(18)\nWA JA-A’LNAA BAYNAHUM WA BAYNA AL-QURAA LATEE BAARAKNAA FEEHAA QORAM ZAAHERATAN WWAQADDARNAA FEEHAA AS-SAYRA SEEROO FEEHAA LAYAALEAAA WA ILLAA AAMENEENA.\nAnd We caused between them and the towns which We had blest, (other) towns to be seen, and We have made easy the journey therein; travel ye through them nights and days, secure.\nفَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا بٰعِدْ بَيْنَ اَسْفَارِنَا وَظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَحَادِيْثَ وَمَزَّقْنٰهُمْ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُوْرٍ‏(19)\nFA-QAALOO RABBANAA BAAE’ED BAYNA AASFAARENAA WA ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM FAJAA’ALNAAHUM AAHAADEESA WAMAZZAQNAAHUM KULLA MUMAZZAQIN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEKULLE SABBAARIN SHAKOORIN.\nThen said they: “O’ our Lord! make the spaces to be longer between our journey” and unjust were they unto themselves, We made them stories and scattered them with a total scattering; Verily in this are signs for every patient, grateful one.\nوَلَقَدْ صَدَّقَ عَلَيْهِمْ اِبْلِيْسُ ظَنَّهٗ فَاتَّبَعُوْهُ اِلَّا فَرِيْقًا مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA LAQAD SADDAQA A’LAYHIM AEBLEESU ZANNAH FAATTABAU’OOHU ILLAA FAREEQAM MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd indeed ‘Iblis’ found true his conjecture concerning them, so they followed him, except a section of the believers.\nوَمَا كَانَ لَهٗ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنٍ اِلَّا لِنَعْلَمَ مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ مِمَّنْ هُوَ مِنْهَا فِىْ شَكٍّ ؕ وَ رَبُّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَفِيْظٌ‏(21)\nWA MAA KAANA LAHU A’LAYHIM MIN SULTAANIN ILLAA ILLAA MAN YOAMENO BIL AAKHERATE MIMMAN HOWA MINHAA FEE SHAKKIM WA RABBOKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN HAFEEZUN.\nAnd there is not for him any authority over them, save that We would know (distinguish) him who believeth in the here after, from him who is in doubt concerning it; and thy Lord is upon all things a Guard.\nقُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِۚ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا لَهُمْ فِيْهِمَا مِنْ شِرْكٍ وَّمَا لَهٗ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ ظَهِيْرٍ‏(22)\nQOLIL ADU’OOA LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAA YAMLEKOONA MISQAALA ZARRATIN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA LAA FIL ARZE WA MAA LAHUM FEEHEMAA MIN SHERKIN WA MAA LAHU MINHUM MIN ZAHEERIN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Call ye upon those whom ye deemed (as gods) besides God; they own not the weight of (even) an atom in the heavens nor in the earth, nor for them is any partnership (share) in either (of them) nor for Him is (there) from among them any one to back up.\nوَلَا تَنْفَعُ الشَّفَاعَةُ عِنْدَهٗۤ اِلَّا لِمَنْ اَذِنَ لَهٗ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا فُزِّعَ عَنْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ قَالُوْا مَاذَا ۙ قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ ؕ قَالُوا الْحَقَّ ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْكَبِيْرُ‏(23)\nWA LAA TANFAU’U ASH-SHAFAAA’ATU I’NDAHU ILLAA LEMAN-Y AZENA LAHU HATTAA EZAA FUZZEA’A A’N QOLOOBEHIM QAALOO MAA QAALA RABBOKUM QAALUD HAQQA WA HOWA A’LIYYUL AL-KABEERU.\nAnd will avail not aught any intercession with Him save of him whom He hath permitted, Until when terror shall be removed from their hearts, they shall say: “What is it that your Lord said?” They (the angels) shall say: “(that which is) True and He is the Most High, the Greatest!\nقُلْ مَنْ يَّرْزُقُكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ ۙ وَ اِنَّاۤ اَوْ اِيَّاكُمْ لَعَلٰى هُدًى اَوْ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(24)\nQUL MAN YARZOQOKUM MENAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ QOLIL LAAHO WA INNAA AW AEEAKUM LAA’ALAA HODAM AW FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nSay thou: “Who provideth you with sustenance from the heavens and the earth?” Say thou: “(It is) God, and verily (either) we or ye are guided aright, or in manifest error?\nقُلْ لَّا تُسْئَلُوْنَ عَمَّاۤ اَجْرَمْنَا وَلَا نُسْئَلُ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(25)\nQUL LAA TUS-ALOONA A’MMAA AAJRAMNAA WA LAA NUSALU A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nSay thou: “Ye will not be questioned as to what we are guilty of, nor shall we be questioned as to what ye do.\nقُلْ يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَنَا رَبُّنَا ثُمَّ يَفْتَحُ بَيْنَنَا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَهُوَ الْفَتَّاحُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(26)\nQUL YAJMAU’U BAYNANAA RABBONAA SUMMA YAFTAHU BAYNANAA BIL-HAQQE WA HOWA AL-FATTAAHU A’LEEM.\nSay thou: “Our Lord will gather us together, then will He judge between us with justice; and He is the Greatest Judge, the All Knowing.\nقُلْ اَرُوْنِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَ لْحَقْتُمْ بِهٖ شُرَكَآءَ كَلَّا ؕ بَلْ هُوَ اللّٰهُ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(27)\nQUL AAROONEAAA LAZEENA A’ZAABAN LHAQTUM BEHI SHORA-KAAA-A KALLAA BAL HOWA LAAHO A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nSay thou: “Show me those whom ye associate with Him: Never (can ye ever do it); Nay! He is God the All-Mighty, the All-Wise.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا كَآفَّةً لِّلنَّاسِ بَشِيْرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(28)\nWA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA KAAAF-FATANW LIN-NAASE BASHEERANW WA NAZEERANW WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) We sent thee not but unto the whole of mankind, a Bearer of glad tidings and a Warner, but most of the people know (it) not.\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd say they: “When will this promise be (fulfilled)? If ye be truthful.\nقُلْ لَّكُمْ مِّيْعَادُ يَوْمٍ لَّا تَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ عَنْهُ سَاعَةً وَّلَا تَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(30)\nQUL LAKUM MMEEA’AADU YAWMIN LAA TASTAAKHEROONA A’NHO SAAA’ATAN WA LAA TASTAQDEMOONA.\nSay thou: “For you is the appointment of a day from which ye cannot hold it back (even) a while, nor can ye hasten it on.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ بِهٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ وَلَا بِالَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِؕ وَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ مَوْقُوْفُوْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْۖۚ يَرْجِعُ بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضِ اۨلْقَوْلَ‌ۚ يَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اَنْتُمْ لَكُنَّا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAN NOAMENA BEHAAZAA QUR-AANE WA LAA BIL-LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WA LAW TARAAA EZIM ZAALEMOON MAWQOOFOONA I’NDAL RABBEHIM YARJE-O’L KHALAA ELAA BAA’ZE QAWLA YAQOOLO LAZEENA TUZ-E’FOO LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA LAWLAA ANTUM LAKUNNAA MUMENEENA.\nAnd say those who disbelieve: “Never will we believe in this Qur’an, nor in that which is before it;” but couldst thou see when the unjust shall be made to stand before their Lord; returning reproaches from one unto another! Those who were despised as weak will say unto those who had prided: “Had it not been for you, we would certainly have been believers.\nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْۤا اَنَحْنُ صَدَدْنٰكُمْ عَنِ الْهُدٰى بَعْدَ اِذْ جَآءَكُمْ بَلْ كُنْتُمْ مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALA LAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA LILLAZEENA TUZ-E’FOO AANAHNU SADADNAAKUM A’NIL HODAA BA’DA IZ JAAA-AKUM BAL KUNTUM MMUJREMEENA.\nThose who had prided shall say unto those who were despised as weak: “What! did we turn you away from the guidance after it had come unto you? Nay! ye were yourselves the guilty ones.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا بَلْ مَكْرُ الَّيْلِ وَ النَّهَارِ اِذْ تَاْمُرُوْنَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّكْفُرَ بِاللّٰهِ وَنَجْعَلَ لَهٗۤ اَنْدَادًا ؕ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّدَامَةَ لَمَّا رَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ ؕ وَجَعَلْنَا الْاَغْلٰلَ فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ هَلْ يُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA TUZ-E’FOO LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA BAL MAKRU LAYLE WA AN-NAHAARE IZ TAAMUROONANAA AN NNAKFURA BIL-LAAHE WANAJA’ALA LAHU ANDAADANW WAASARROOA AN-NADAAMATA LAMMAA RAAWUA A’ZAABA WA JA-A’LNAA AL-AAGHLAALA FEE AAA’NAAQE LAZEENA KAFAROO HAL YUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAnd those who were despised as weak shall say unto those who had prided: “Nay! (it was) (your) planning by night and by day, when ye bade us that we should disbelieve in God and set up equals unto Him.” And they shall feel regretful when they shall see the chastisement; And We will put shackles on the necks of those who disbelieved; They are recompensed aught save what they did.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا فِىْ قَرْيَةٍ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ اِلَّا قَالَ مُتْرَفُوْهَاۤ ۙاِنَّا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلْتُمْ بِهٖ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA FEE QARYATINW MIN NAZEERIM ILLAA QAALA MUTRAFOOHAA INNAA BEMAA URSILTUM BEHI KAAFEROON.\nAnd We sent not a warner unto a town but the opulent ones of it said: “Verily we are disbelievers in what ye are sent with\nوَ قَالُوْا نَحْنُ اَكْثَرُ اَمْوَالًا وَّاَوْلَادًا ۙ وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‏(35)\nWA QAALOO NAHNO AAKSARU AAMWAALAN WWAAWLAADAN WA MAA NAHNO BEMUA’AZZABEENA.\nAnd said they: “We are more (than you) in wealth and in children, and we shall not be the chastised\nقُلْ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(36)\nQUL INNAL RABBEE YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad?): “Verily my Lord amplifieth the sustenance for whomsoever He willeth and straiteneth (it) (for whomsoever He pleaseth), but most of the people know not.\nوَمَاۤ اَمْوَالُكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُكُمْ بِالَّتِىْ تُقَرِّبُكُمْ عِنْدَنَا زُلْفٰٓى اِلَّا مَنْ اٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ جَزَآءُ الضِّعْفِ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا وَهُمْ فِى الْغُرُفٰتِ اٰمِنُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA MAA AMWAALOKUM WA LAA LAA AWLAADOKUM BIL-LATEE TUQARREBUKUM E’ENDANAA ZULFAAA ILLAA MAN AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM JAZAAA-O AZ-ZEA’FE BEMAA A’MELOO WA HUM FIL AL-GHURUFAATE AAMENOON.\nAnd neither your wealth and nor your children are that which bring you nigh unto Us, but whosoever believeth and doeth good, these are, (the ones) for whom is a double recompense for what they do, and they in the exalted places shall be secure.\nوَ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْعَوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا مُعٰجِزِيْنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِى الْعَذَابِ مُحْضَرُوْنَ‏(38)\nWA LAZEENA YASA’AWNA FEE AAYAATENAA MUA’AAJEZEENA OOLAAA-EKA FIL A’ZAABE MOHZAROON.\nAnd those who strive hard in invalidating Our signs, they shall be brought to the chastisement.\nقُلْ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَقْدِرُ لَهٗ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَنْفَقْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَهُوَ يُخْلِفُهٗ ۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(39)\nQUL INNAL RABBEE YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA LAHU WA MAA ANFAQTUM MIN SHAY-IN FAHOWA YUKHLEFUH WA HOWA KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nSay thou: “Verily my Lord amplifieth the sustenance for whomsoever He willeth of His servants and straiteneth (it) for him (whomsoever He pleaseth), and whatever thing ye spend, He returneth it (with His reward along with it), and He is the Best of Sustainers.\nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ يَقُوْلُ لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اَهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اِيَّاكُمْ كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(40)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A SUMMA YAQOOLO LIL-MALAAA-EKATE AAHAAAULAAE AEEAKUM KAANOO YA’BODOON.\nAnd on the day when He will gather them all together, then will He say unto the angels: “Did these worship you?\nقَالُوْا سُبْحٰنَكَ اَنْتَ وَلِيُّنَا مِنْ دُوْنِهِمْۚ بَلْ كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَ الْجِنَّ ۚ اَكْثَرُهُمْ بِهِمْ مُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(41)\nQAALOO SUBHAANAKA ANTA WALEENAA MIN DOONEHEM BAL KAANOO YA’BODOON AL-JENNA AKSAROHUM BEHIM REJAALUM.\nThey shall say: “Glory be to Thee! Thou art our Guardian, not they; Nay! they worshipped the jinn; most of them were the believers in them.\nفَالْيَوْمَ لَا يَمْلِكُ بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ نَّفْعًا وَّلَا ضَرًّا ؕ وَنَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ النَّارِ الَّتِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(42)\nFALYAWMA LAA YAMLEKU BA’ZOKUM LE-BA’ZIN NNAFA’AN WA LAA BEKUM WANAQOOLU LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL NAAR LATEE KUNTUM BEHAA TOKAZZEBOON.\nSo on that day shall not own one of you for the other any profit or harm; and We will say unto those who did injustice: “Taste ye the chastisement of the fire which ye did disbelieve.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالُوْا مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا رَجُلٌ يُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّصُدَّكُمْ عَمَّا كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ‌ ۚ وَقَالُوْا مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِفْكٌ مُّفْتَرً ىؕ وَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ ۙ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(43)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT QAALOO MAA HAAZAA ILLAA RAJOLUM YYUREEDU AN YYASUDDAKUM A’MMAA KAANA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUKUM WA QAALOO MAA HAAZAA ILLAA AEFKUN MMUFTARAN AA WA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nAnd when are recited unto them Our clear signs say they: “This is none but a man, desireth he to turn ye away from what your fathers did worship,” and say they: “This (Qur’an) is naught but a falsehood forged” and those who disbelieve say of the truth when it cometh unto them: “This is nothing but a clear sorcery.\nوَمَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ كُتُبٍ يَّدْرُسُوْنَهَا وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمْ قَبْلَكَ مِنْ نَّذِيْرٍؕ‏(44)\nWA MAA AATAYNAAHUM MIN KUTUBIN YYADRUSOONAHAA WA MAA ARSALNAA ELAYHIM QABLAKA MIN NNAZEERIN.\nAnd We have not given them any books which they read, nor did We send unto them before thee any warner.\nوَكَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْۙ وَمَا بَلَغُوْا مِعْشَارَ مَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ فَكَذَّبُوْا رُسُلِىْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ نَكِيْرِ‏(45)\nWA KAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA MAA BALAGHOOA MEA’SHAARA MAA AATAYNAAHUM FA KAZZABOO RUSULEAA FA-KAYFA KAANA NAKEER.\nAnd belied those before them and these have not attained (even) the tithe of what We gave them, and yet they belied My apostles; so how (intense) was My abhorrence (of them).\nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَعِظُكُمْ بِوَاحِدَةٍ ۚ اَنْ تَقُوْمُوْا لِلّٰهِ مَثْنٰى وَفُرَادٰى ثُمَّ تَتَفَكَّرُوْا مَا بِصَاحِبِكُمْ مِّنْ جِنَّةٍ ؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ لَّكُمْ بَيْنَ يَدَىْ عَذَابٍ شَدِيْدٍ‏(46)\nQUL INNAMAA AAE’EZUKUM BEWAAHEDATIN AN TAQOOMOOA LILLAAHE MASNAA WAFURAADAA SUMMA TATAFAKKAROOA MAA BESAAHEBEKUM MIN JENNATIN IN HOWA ILLAA NAZEERUM LAKUM BAYNA YADAY A’ZAABIN BAA-SIN.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I exhort you only to one thing, that rise up ye for God’s sake in twos and singly, then ponder ye: your companion (Our Apostle Muhammad) is not possessed, he is none but a warner (sent) unto you, before a severe chastisement.\nقُلْ مَا سَاَ لْتُكُمْ مِّنْ اَجْرٍ فَهُوَ لَكُمْ ؕ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ ۚ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(47)\nQUL MAA HAQ LTUKUM MIN AAJRIN FAHOWA LAKUM IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WA.\nSay thou: “Whatever recompense I have asked of you, it is only for yourselves; my recompense is (to be expected) from God (alone), and He is witness over all things.\nقُلْ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ يَقْذِفُ بِالْحَقِّ‌ۚ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ‏(48)\nQUL INNAL RABBEE YAQZEFU BIL-HAQQE A’ALLAAMU AL-GHUYOOBE.\nSay thou: “Verily my Lord doth hurleth (out) the (light of) Truth, The Greatest Knower of the unseen.\nقُلْ جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَمَا يُبْدِئُ الْبَاطِلُ وَمَا يُعِيْدُ‏(49)\nQUL JAAA-A HAQQO WA MAA YUBDEO BAATELO WA MAA YUE’EEDU.\nSay thou: “The truth hath come, and falsehood neither bringeth forth anything nor doth it reproduce.\nقُلْ اِنْ ضَلَلْتُ فَاِنَّمَاۤ اَضِلُّ عَلٰى نَفْسِىْ ۚ وَاِنِ اهْتَدَيْتُ فَبِمَا يُوْحِىْۤ اِلَىَّ رَبِّىْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ سَمِيْعٌ قَرِيْبٌ‏(50)\nQUL IN ZALALTU FA-INNAMAA AAZELLU A’LAA NAFSEE WA ENIS AHTADAYTU FA BEMAA YOOHEAA ELAYYA RABBEE INNAHU SAMEE-U’N QAREEB.\nSay thou: “If I stray, I stray only against my own self, and if I am guided aright, it is of what hath revealed unto me my Lord; Verily He is All-Hearing, the (Most) Nigh.\nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ فَزِعُوْا فَلَا فَوْتَ وَاُخِذُوْا مِنْ مَّكَانٍ قَرِيْبٍۙ‏(51)\nWA LAW TARAAA IZ FAZEU’OOA FALAA FAWTA WA OKHEZOO MIN MAKAANIM QAREEBIN.\nAnd couldst thou see when they shall get terrified, then there shall be no escape and they shall be seized from a near place,\nوَّقَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِهٖ‌ ۚ وَاَنّٰى لَهُمُ التَّنَاوُشُ مِنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ ۖۚ‏(52)\nWA QAALOO AAMANNAA BEHI INSAANO WA LAHOMUL AT-TANAAWUSHU MIN MAKAANIM BA-E’ED.\nAnd they shall say: “We (now) believe in it.” And whence shall the approach (to faith) be for them from (such) a distant place?\nوَّقَدْ كَفَرُوْا بِهٖ مِنْ قَبْلُۚ وَيَقْذِفُوْنَ بِالْغَيْبِ مِنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‌‏(53)\nWWAQAD KAFAROO BEHI MIN QABLO WAYAQZEFOONA BIL-GHAYBE MIN MAKAANIM BA-E’ED.\nAnd indeed they did disbelieve in it before, and aim their conjectures about the unseen from a distant place.\nوَحِيْلَ بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ مَا يَشْتَهُوْنَ كَمَا فُعِلَ بِاَشْيَاعِهِمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا فِىْ شَكٍّ مُّرِيْبٍ‏(54)\nWAHEELA BAYNAHUM WA BAYNA MAA YASHTAHOONA KAMAA FUE’ELA BEAASHYAAE’EHEM MIN QABL WA INNAHUM KAANOO FEE SHAKKIM MMUREEBIN.\nAnd a gulf shall be set between them and that which they desire, as was done unto the likes of them of yore, verily they have been in a disquieting doubt.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Sabaa\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 54 verses. It is narrated that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that whoever recites this Surah, on the Day of Judgement, all the Prophets and Messengers will come to meet him.\nIn a saying from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) it is mentioned that whoever recites Surah Sabaa and [Surah Faatir](A39) at night, he will remain under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) for the whole night. The reward for reciting this Surah is so great that when it is seen in the book of deeds, the reciter’s heart will be filled with joy.\nWearing this Surah as a talisman or drinking its water removes fear from one’s heart and keeps one safe from enemies and wild animals."
}
